# Changelog

All notable changes to this project are documented in this file.

## [Unreleased]

### Added

#### Phase 4.1 — Core Foundation
- Managed byte buffer standard library (`@std/buffers/buffer.dryad`): bounds-checked allocation, byte read/write/fill, zero-copy slicing over parent buffers, resize, copy, and UTF-8 string conversion via `Buffer_FromString`/`Buffer_AsString`.
- Memory intrinsics (`syscall.alloc_bytes`, `syscall.free_bytes`, `syscall.buffer_get`, `syscall.buffer_set`, `syscall.memcpy`, `syscall.memset`) backed by a bounds-checked `MemoryManager`.
- String intrinsics (`syscall.string_length`, `syscall.string_to_bytes`, `syscall.bytes_to_string`) for UTF-8 bytes <-> string roundtrips.
- Virtual filesystem (`@std/io/vfs.dryad`): MemoryBackend listing and a NativeBackend that reads, writes, removes, lists, and creates directories through filesystem syscalls.
- High-level I/O (`@std/io/file.dryad`) and FileHandle lifecycle (`@std/io/filehandle.dryad`), including append mode.
- Filesystem helpers: `syscall.exists`, `syscall.filesize`, `syscall.readdir`, `syscall.open_read` / `open_write` / `open_append`, `syscall.string_starts_with`, `runtime.object_keys`, `runtime.array_push`.
- `import { ... } from "@std/..."` module loading with transitive stdlib resolution.
- CLI script execution: `dryad script.dryad`, plus `--help` and `--version`.
- POO: `abstract class`, `super`, properties (`readonly`, `abstract readonly`), `interface`/`implements`, semantic validator (`dryad check`).
- LSP foundation: explicit `get`/`set` accessors, multiple diagnostics, parser error recovery, basic type validation.

#### Phase 4.2 — File I/O & Streams
- `@std/io/stream.dryad` abstract Stream API; `@std/core/disposable.dryad` as real interface.
- `FileStream` extending `Stream`, `FileMode`, `File_open`/`File_exists`/`File_delete`/`File_readAllText`/`File_writeAllText`.
- `MemoryStream`, `Path` utilities (`@std/io/path.dryad`), auto-create parent dirs on `File_open`.
- `Stream_isStream`/`Stream_isError` helpers; async file wrappers via `Promise_resolve`.
- Examples: `examples/stream_usage.dryad`.

#### Phase 4.3 — Collections
- `@std/core/enumerable.dryad` — `IEnumerable` interface.
- `@std/collections`: `List`, `Map`, `Set`, `Queue` with barrel module `@std/collections`.
- Example: `examples/collections_usage.dryad`.

#### Phase 4.4 — Networking (TCP)
- Network syscalls: `socket`, `connect`, `bind`, `listen`, `accept`, `send`/`recv`, `send_buffer`/`recv_buffer`, `shutdown`, `getsockname`, `set_reuseaddr`, `get_errno`.
- `--allow-net` CLI flag and `DRYAD_ALLOW_NET=1` env gate for network access.
- `@std/net`: `Socket`, `NetworkStream`, `TcpClient`, `TcpListener`, `net_errors`.
- Example: `examples/net_echo_client.dryad`.
- Architecture plan: `docs/implementation/plans/2026-09-16-net-architecture.md`.

#### Phase 4.5 — Async, UDP, DNS, TLS, HTTP
- `@std/async/promise.dryad` — `Promise<T>` with deferred `then()` callback queues, `Promise_all`, `Promise_race`, `catchError`, `finallyDo`.
- `@std/async/threading/` — `Thread`, `Thread_parallel`, `ThreadPool`, `ThreadPool_map` (OS threads, blocking join model).
- C++ runtime: `ThreadManager`, `intrinsics_thread.cpp` (`__thread_spawn`, `__thread_join`, `__thread_pool_*`, `__thread_sleep_ms`, `__thread_hardware_concurrency`).
- UDP: `syscall.sendto_buffer`, `syscall.recvfrom_buffer`; `@std/net/udp_client.dryad`.
- DNS: `syscall.resolve_host`; `@std/net/dns.dryad`.
- TLS (optional OpenSSL, `DRYAD_ENABLE_TLS=ON`): `tls_client_handshake`, `tls_send_buffer`, `tls_recv_buffer`, `tls_close`, `tls_available`; `@std/net/tls_stream.dryad`.
- HTTP client: `@std/net/http/*` (`http_url`, `http_headers`, `http_request`, `http_response`, `http_client`).
- `@std/net/socket_async.dryad` — Promise wrappers over blocking socket I/O.
- Utils: `syscall.int_to_string`, `runtime.value_kind`.

### Changed
- Repository split into modules: the implementation now lives in `src/`; documentation, runnable examples and the language specification live in the `docs` submodule (`github.com/dryadlang/docs`).
- The superseded Rust-era `archived/` tree was removed.
- Example-based tests read scripts from `docs/examples` (with a local `src/examples` fallback).

### Fixed
- POSIX compatibility for MSYS2/Windows builds (intrinsic handle width and file open flags).
- Class method calls now bind `this` when invoking instance methods (`obj.method()`).
- Constructors use module closure (not caller env) for `new` lookups in collections.
- `Net_socketError` — removed invalid integer+string concatenation.
- HTTP/DNS/path helpers — fixed `__string_to_bytes` misuse in `Http_charAt` and similar byte-index helpers.
- Thread pool deadlock — `pool_wait` no longer holds global mutex while worker initializes interpreter.
- Thread pool race — workers hold `shared_ptr<ThreadJob>` from queue instead of map lookup after `wait()` erases entry.

### Known limitations
- `catch` / `finally` are reserved keywords → Promise uses `catchError` / `finallyDo`.
- Promise model is synchronous (no real event loop); `then()` queues callbacks for pending promises.
- Threading uses blocking `start()` + `join()`; each worker runs a separate `Interpreter`.
- TLS is client-only with no rigorous certificate verification.
- Dryad `&&` does not short-circuit — use nested `if` in tests/scripts.

### Tests
- **344 unit + 18 integration tests passing (100%)**
- New suites: collections, filestream, memory_stream, path, enumerable, list/map/set/queue, network, socket, udp, http_client, promise, threading, language_features.
- Integration: collections workflow, file I/O workflow, net echo, HTTP smoke, UDP echo, HTTP client.
